Theta arithmetic
================

`prism-isogeny/src/theta.rs` ports the theta-coordinate doubling from
`external/PRISM_v2/src/hd/ref/lvlx/theta_structure.c` and the inline
transforms in `theta_structure.h`.

`prism-isogeny/src/theta_step.rs` and `prism-isogeny/src/splitting.rs` port
the (2,2)-step, the splitting isomorphism, and the product-to-Montgomery
maps from `theta_isogenies.c`, and the splitting-matrix table from
`src/precomp/ref/lvl1/hd_splitting_transforms.c`. The signing-only
normalisation matrices are not included: verification calls splitting with
randomisation off.

`prism-isogeny/src/jac.rs` ports Jacobian doubling and addition, and the
basis lift, from `src/ec/ref/lvlx/ec_jac.c` and `basis.c`.

`prism-isogeny/src/modular.rs` is the closed form of the dim-2 symplectic
matrices whose block equations are `complete_symplectic_matrix_dim2` in
`external/Theta_dim4` `pkg/basis_change/base_change_dim2.py`
(Apache-2.0, Pierrick Dartois). `prism-isogeny/src/theta_base.rs` ports
`base_change_theta_dim2` from that file. The adapted dim-2 chain and its dual evaluation are ported in
`prism-isogeny/src/dual_chain.rs`. The files `isogeny_chain_dim2.py`,
`gluing_isogeny_dim2.py`, and `isogeny_dim2.py` additionally carry the MIT
notice of Pierrick Dartois, Luciano Maino, Giacomo Pope and Damien Robert
(2023). That notice is retained in `LICENSES/Theta_dim2-MIT.txt`; the
Theta_dim4 Apache-2.0 license is in `LICENSES/Theta_dim4-Apache-2.0.txt`.

`prism-isogeny/src/gluing.rs` and `prism-isogeny/src/chain.rs` port the
gluing isogeny and `_theta_chain_compute_impl` from `theta_isogenies.c`.
The signing-only randomisation of the final model is not included.

That code is Apache-2.0. Its authors, as named in those files, are
Antonin Leroux and the SQIsign authors. The PRISM_v2 repository
(https://github.com/mariascrs/PRISM_v2, commit
87fad7da5f12f79112521677f4f5530672afe9ba) carries the same license and
states that it is built on Qlapoti and the SQIsign reference.

The rest of this repository is BSD-3-Clause, The Shekyl Foundation.

Research comparison and protocol framing
========================================

The salted cSHAKE framing and caller-randomness schedule are the local
research protocol in docs/SALT_PROTOCOL.md. They are not the upstream
C wire format. prism-compare retains the Foundation's archived unsalted
framing and original public fixture data for reproducible comparisons.
The low-level isogeny implementations and their notices above are unchanged.
